  BUG: stats.beta.entropy: doesn't work with array-valued a, b
### Describe your issue.

Beta distribution entropy doesn't work with array-valued a, b

### Reproducing Code Example

```python
import numpy as np
import scipy.stats as ss
beta = ss.make_distribution(ss.beta)
b = beta(a=np.zeros(10), b=np.ones(10))
b.entropy()
```

